  "question": {
    "html": "<p>A sealed container that is thermally isolated from its environment contains water at <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"85\"></span> <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"^{\\circ}\"></span>C and ice at <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"-10\"></span> <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"^{\\circ}\"></span>C. What is true about the total internal energy of the system?</p>\n<p></p>\n<ol class=\"mcq-options\">\n<li data-label=\"A\">It increases.</li>\n<li data-label=\"B\">It decreases.</li>\n<li data-label=\"C\">It remains unchanged.</li>\n<li data-label=\"D\">It increases until the ice and the water reach the same temperature and then it remains unchanged.</li>\n</ol>"
  },
